#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:8
msgid "A program is converted into scheduled runs, checked against current restrictions, and then operates the master and station outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:9
msgid "Every requested run must pass the system, mode, rain, sensor, and station availability checks before an output is energized."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:10
msgid "A station assigned to a master observes the configured lead and lag delays while OSPy coordinates both outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:11
msgid "The selected weather provider is normalized into one cached data model used by water-level calculations, programs, Home, and plug-ins."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:12
msgid "Measurements are discovered or received, validated, stored, evaluated against rules, and may stop irrigation or create notifications."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:13
msgid "A plug-in must pass its manifest, compatibility, permission, and pre-activation checks before ordered startup and health monitoring."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:14
msgid "An update is fetched from the selected channel, checked, installed, restarted, and confirmed by the watchdog or rolled back."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:15
msgid "Settings use verified atomic SQLite writes with a synchronized shelve/DBM fallback and recovery path."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:16
msgid "Backup creation and restore validate the complete archive, preserve a safety copy, restart OSPy, and verify the result."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:17
msgid "A web request passes transport, authentication, brute-force, second-factor, role, and CSRF checks before OSPy serves or changes protected data."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:18
msgid "HTTPS uses the selected certificate source to establish an encrypted connection; invalid files or trust failures are reported without pretending that the transport is secure."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:19
msgid "After the password, OSPy loads the built-in administrator or additional user’s independent 2FA settings and verifies a TOTP, e-mail, or one-time backup code before creating the session."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:20
msgid "The mobile application reaches the saved OSPy installation over its configured local or remote HTTPS address, authenticates through Mobile API v1, reads current state, sends permitted actions, and updates the screen from the response."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:21
msgid "OSPy matches an event to registered phone preferences, queues and signs an HTTPS relay request, and the relay delivers it through Firebase Cloud Messaging to Android even while the OSPy application is closed."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:22
msgid "Session and CSRF tokens protect web actions, while optional remember-me tokens store only a hash and can expire or be revoked."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:23
msgid "API and sensor requests apply configured Basic authentication, throttling, roles, CSRF, and browser CORS rules before data are accepted or an action is executed."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:24
msgid "Scheduled, manual, and run-once requests share a prioritized queue that respects output capacity, group order, and station delays."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:25
msgid "Rain sensing, rain delay, normalized forecasts, and the stored water balance decide whether a weather-aware run is skipped or receives an adjusted duration."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:26
msgid "An output request is mapped through the configured backend, polarity, and master sequence; driver acknowledgement does not by itself prove that a physical relay switched."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:27
msgid "Anonymous, operator, and administrator roles are checked for every protected route and action, independently of authentication and CSRF validation."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:28
msgid "Operational events, active recoverable problems, diagnostic modals, persistent incidents, and technical debug tracebacks form separate but connected reporting layers."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:29
msgid "Configured events are composed into localized notifications, enriched with optional station and sensor data, and sent through the selected provider with bounded retry and error logging."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:30
msgid "OSPy starts settings, safe outputs, core workers, and dependency-ordered plug-ins before reporting readiness; shutdown reverses that process and leaves outputs off."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:31
msgid "Declared plug-in permissions are compared with the approved set, reviewed when they change, persisted with an audit event, and checked before any plug-in code starts."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:32
msgid "A sensor is discovered, identified independently of its changing IP address, validated, monitored for stale data, evaluated against rules, and recorded with any resulting action."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:33
msgid "Local and Internet clients reach OSPy through different network boundaries; Internet exposure should combine a restricted firewall or VPN, trusted HTTPS, and strong authentication."
msgstr ""

#: ospy/templates/diagnostics.html:34
msgid "A clean installation validates the platform, preserves existing checkouts, installs the stable master branch and selected dependencies, verifies SQLite and systemd, and confirms the first secure login."
msgstr ""

