msgstr ""

#: plugins/rs485_communication/templates/rs485_communication_help.html:62
msgid "Connect RS485 B- to B / D- / 485- of the target device."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/rs485_communication/templates/rs485_communication_help.html:63
msgid "Connect GND when required by the installation and the target device documentation."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/rs485_communication/templates/rs485_communication_help.html:66
msgid "Port selection"
msgstr ""

#: plugins/rs485_communication/templates/rs485_communication_help.html:67
msgid "The default value auto searches specifically for a WCH CH343G adapter. On Raspberry Pi it normally appears as /dev/ttyACM0. You can also enter a fixed path manually, including a /dev/serial/by-id path."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/rs485_communication/templates/rs485_communication_help.html:70
msgid "The selected baud rate and serial format apply to the complete physical bus. All devices connected to the same A/B pair normally have to use the same values. The default 4800 8N1 matches the documented factory setting of the ZTS-3000-FSJT wind sensor."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/rs485_communication/templates/rs485_communication_help.html:71
msgid "Saving a new speed changes how OSPy opens the USB adapter; it does not change a slave device. A device-specific plug-in must first send the documented configuration command and then switch the bus to the same speed."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/rs485_communication/templates/rs485_communication_help.html:71
#: plugins/rs485_communication/templates/rs485_communication_help.html:75
msgid "Important"
msgstr ""

#: plugins/rs485_communication/templates/rs485_communication_help.html:73
msgid "Adapter test"
msgstr ""

#: plugins/rs485_communication/templates/rs485_communication_help.html:74
msgid "The Test adapter button verifies that the USB serial adapter is detected and that OSPy can open the selected serial port with the configured parameters. The test intentionally sends no arbitrary bytes to the live RS485 bus."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/rs485_communication/templates/rs485_communication_help.html:75
msgid "A successful adapter test does not prove A/B wiring or communication with a slave device. A complete RS485 line test requires a responding device or a second RS485 adapter."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/rs485_communication/templates/rs485_communication_help.html:77
msgid "RS485 queue"
msgstr ""

#: plugins/rs485_communication/templates/rs485_communication_help.html:78
msgid "All dependent plug-ins should use the public rs485_queue object. Requests are processed in FIFO order by one worker, so two plug-ins cannot transmit on the half-duplex RS485 bus at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/rs485_communication/templates/rs485_communication_help.html:80
msgid "Synchronous transaction"
msgstr ""

#: plugins/rs485_communication/templates/rs485_communication_help.html:89
msgid "Asynchronous queued transaction"
msgstr ""

#: plugins/rs485_communication/templates/rs485_communication_help.html:99
msgid "Atomic multi-step protocol"
msgstr ""

#: plugins/rs485_communication/templates/rs485_communication_help.html:100
msgid "Use call() when one protocol operation needs several writes and reads. The callback runs entirely inside the RS485 worker and remains atomic with respect to other queued plug-ins."
msgstr ""

#: plugins/rs485_communication/templates/rs485_communication_help.html:114
msgid "The settings page shows the current queue depth, active queue client, completed/error counters, peak queue depth and the last queue waiting time."
msgstr ""

